char *protocol_base64_decode(const char *data, size_t *outlen);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Decodes a NUL\-terminated base64 string into binary data.
The returned buffer is heap\-allocated with \f[CR]malloc(3)\f[R] and
NUL\-terminated (the NUL is not counted in \f[CR]*outlen\f[R]).
The caller is responsible for freeing the returned buffer.
.PP
The input must use the standard base64 alphabet
(\f[CR]A\-Za\-z0\-9+/\f[R]) with \f[CR]=\f[R] padding.
The input length must be a multiple of 4; otherwise, decoding fails.
.PP
Invalid characters (bytes not in the base64 alphabet and not
\f[CR]=\f[R]) in the first two positions of any 4\-byte group cause the
function to fail and return NULL.
.PP
A static 256\-byte lookup table is lazily initialized on the first call.
